Package: spherepack
Type: Package
Title: Spherical Harmonic Analysis, Synthesis, and Differential Operators
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Takeshi", "Enomoto", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "takeshi.enomoto@gmail.com"),
    person("John", "Adams", role = "aut", comment = "SPHEREPACK 3.2 author"),
    person("Paul", "Swarztrauber", role = "aut", comment = "SPHEREPACK 3.2 author"),
    person("University Corporation for Atmospheric Research", role = "cph", comment = "SPHEREPACK 3.2 copyright holder")
  )
Description: Provides an R interface to the 'SPHEREPACK' 3.2 Fortran 77 library
  (Adams and Swarztrauber, 1999) for spherical harmonic analysis and synthesis
  of scalar and vector fields, as well as divergence, vorticity, stream function,
  velocity potential, gradient, scalar and vector Laplacians, inverse operators,
  latitudinal derivatives, spectral truncation, and exponential tapering on
  global equally spaced (fixed) and Gaussian grids. Function names and behavior
  are compatible with the NCAR Command Language (NCL) spherical harmonic routines
  while leveraging the column-major array layout shared between Fortran and R.
